Subject: vfs: a base file's descriptor lives only while a handle holds it open, and a recovery reopens only the base root (slates A-832 942d4a37e, A-833 6e3dec78d)
Why: Every Slates daemon kept one file descriptor per base file it ever read and never closed it: kiln's daemon on adacachy reached 1,048,575 of 1,048,576 and refused every open, so kiln's up() failed and the anchor exited 4; this MacBook's held 4,574. Its restart then reopened ~192,000 recorded base directories in one step and the liveness watchdog killed it a second in, every time. Both are fixed on Slates main (A-832, A-833), with their tests; this carries them until the next re-vendor, which drops this change as upstream's own.

